  "result": "The gate returned **OK** on its second run of six: 15 witnesses pass and the rule declares 2 narrowings of my own.\n\n**Run 1 (VACUOUS):** three checks inside the \"a bus or taxicab is waiting or about to enter the zone\" exception never changed any witness's verdict. They are whether that vehicle occupies the zone, whether it is within 10 m of it, and whether it is halted. I added `branch_11`. In it, three motor vehicles of unresolved bus/taxicab class sit near the subject while it loads, and each is placed so one of those checks decides the result. One is at rest inside the zone, one is at rest 37.7 m beyond it, and one creeps away and leaves the 10 m reach without entering. **Run 2: OK.**\n\n**The rule:** it applies when a vehicle occupies a bus stop and is not a bus, or a taxicab stand and is not a taxicab. In that zone it must not halt, unless one of three things holds:\n- **Queue:** another road user is ahead in its lane within 5 m.\n- **Device or officer:** its lane is governed by a stop sign, a yield sign, a red or yellow signal, an active railway signal or gate, or a police officer signalling stop.\n- **Passenger stop:** it is a passenger vehicle, the stop is shorter than 60 s, a door opens during the halt, and no bus or taxicab was waiting to enter or about to enter the zone during the halt.\n\n**Two choices of mine, both declared as narrowings on s1:**\n- **Signal colours:** \"a red or yellow indication\" means steady red or yellow, circular or arrow, plus flashing red. Flashing yellow doesn't count.\n- **Railway gate:** \"gate not up\" means lowering, down or raising. A device with no gate doesn't count.\n\n**Reading limitation (worth passing to the plan):** in this run's reading, the bus and taxicab definitions include no vehicle class. So:\n- No road user can ever be decidedly a bus or a taxicab. The \"waiting or about to enter\" exception is therefore only ever false or unknown, and can never by itself make a halt a violation.\n- No vehicle can be decidedly \"not a taxicab\", so the rule can never be decided to apply in a taxicab stand.\n\nThat's why every witness uses a taxicab-class car in a bus stop: it is decidedly not a bus, so the rule applies to it.\n\nFiles:\n- `library/TrafficSpec/Rules/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_517.lean`\n- `library/TrafficSpecWitness/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_517.lean`\n- `results/full221-1116-1018/iter-003/code/NRS_484B_517/task_result.md`",
